<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel Engineering '96 profit falls.</title>
<headline>Keppel Engineering '96 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  10.85  vs  14.41</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		   2.00  vs   2.50</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)		5.40  vs   7.20</p>
<p>    Turnover			   314.25  vs 280.10</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 2.10  vs   1.73</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	  3.17  vs   3.71</p>
<p>    Other income			 2.53  vs   3.01</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    20.06  vs  22.88</p>
<p>    Tax				    3.31  vs   5.14</p>
<p>    Minorities		  loss  (1.39) vs   0.33 gain</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	   loss  (9.39) vs    nil</p>
<p>Note: Keppel Integrated Engineering Ltd (KIE), said the extraordinary item comprises provisions for closure losses of non-viable businesses in associates.</p>
<p>KIE is a unit of diversified marine conglomerate Keppel Corp .</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
